// WHERE THE SUCCESS PAIRS COME FROM, since this is the one part of the minigame the wiki does not
// publish: Old School gives every tier's level, experience and favour, and says only that the gem
// machetes "chop faster". So the pairs are built the way the woodcutting table's are - low is the
// chance at level 1 and high the chance at 99, out of 256, fed to stat_random - and set so that:
//
//   a plain machete at the tier's own level lands roughly one swing in three, which is what a tree
//   of the same requirement does in this build (the normal tree is 64/200 at level 1);
//   each gem blade is about a fifth faster than the one below it, in the order the cache lists
//   them - opal, jade, red topaz;
//   and dense jungle at 99 with a red topaz machete is close to every swing, because that is what
//   99 Woodcutting does to a yew.
//
// The three tiers' own numbers - 10/20/35 and 32/55/80 xp and 0.3/0.5/1.0% - are Old School's.
// https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Tai_Bwo_Wannai_Cleanup

[tbwcu_jungle_light]
